%[text] Explore the[ Medical Ventilator With Lung Model ](https://www.mathworks.com/help/simscape/ug/medical-ventilator-with-lung-model.html)example.
%[text] 1. Open the model \
openExample('simscape/MedicalVentilatorWithLungModelExample')
%[text] If you would like to change the model parameters, select the 
%[text] ![](text:image:9e6f)
%[text] Double click on the expiratory tube to adjust block parameters:
%[text] ![](text:image:3ecb)
%[text] 
%%
%[text] 2\. Run the model
%[text] 3\. Go to 'Plot Condensation in expiratory tube (see code)'.
%[text] See code will open, MedicalVentilatorWithLungModelPlot2Condensation.m
%[text] In lines 48 and 49, 
%[text] ![](text:image:8660)
%[text] enter the following code:
%[text] ```matlabCodeExample
%[text] save("CondenseDat.mat","t","V");
%[text] ```
%[text] Remove data points from the code and add Gaussian noise with the following code.
% Code to generate noisy ventilator data from 
load CondenseDat.mat t V

t = t(1:30:end); % Take every 100th point of t
V = V(1:30:end); % Take every 100th point of V
% Add noise to the V data
noiseLevel = .005; % Increase the noise level for more variation
V = V + noiseLevel * randn(size(V)); % Add Gaussian noise
% Plot the sampled data


